---
scope: src/tools/upgrade/buildVersionsMeta
status: misaligned
description: >
  Build-time script that generates a complete versions.json manifest covering all AIDE artifact categories, shipped as a static asset inside the published npm package.
intent: >
  buildVersionsMeta is a build-time script that produces a versions.json
  manifest containing version metadata for every artifact the MCP server
  delivers to host projects — methodology docs, commands, agents, skills,
  and extensions. The manifest is generated during the npm publish pipeline,
  baked into the package as a static asset, and read by both aide_init and
  aide_upgrade at runtime. Host projects never need access to the MCP
  server's git history or source repo; the manifest travels with the
  package.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - "versions.json contains an entry for every deliverable artifact across all categories: methodology docs, commands, agents, skills, and extensions. No category is silently omitted."
    - "Each entry carries enough metadata to identify the version of that artifact (publication timestamp, source commit reference) so consuming tools can detect drift between what the host has and what the package ships."
    - "The manifest is generated at build time during the npm publish pipeline and committed or embedded into the published package as a static file — it is never computed at runtime on the client machine."
    - "Both aide_init and aide_upgrade read the same shipped versions.json to deliver version metadata to host projects."
  undesired:
    - "Runtime dependency on git availability or the MCP server's repo history on the client machine. Clients install from npm and have no access to the source repo's git log."
    - "Coverage limited to methodology docs only. Commands, agents, skills, and extensions must be included — a manifest that tracks only docs is incomplete and will miss drift in the majority of delivered artifacts."
    - "An empty or partial versions.json reaching published packages because the build script failed silently or was skipped in the publish pipeline."
    - "aide_init delivering artifacts without version metadata while aide_upgrade delivers it. Both channels must use the same manifest."
---
